    "pmid": "43061418",
    "doi": "10.17912/micropub.biology.002460",
    "title": "Endogenous Expression and Localization of Peroxisome Marker DAAO-1 in Caenorhabditis elegans."
  },
  "content": {
    "abstract": "Peroxisomes coordinate fatty acid beta-oxidation and cellular redox homeostasis. D-amino-acid oxidase (DAAO) is a key peroxisomal matrix enzyme, yet the endogenous subcellular localization of C. elegans DAAO-1 remains uncharacterized. Here, we generated an endogenous mScarlet::daao-1 knock-in strain via CRISPR/Cas9. Confocal microscopy reveals that mScarlet::DAAO-1 localizes exclusively to discrete puncta throughout the intestinal tract from L1 larvae to adulthood. These puncta are spatially distinct from autofluorescent gut granules within the same cells and tissues. This knock-in strain provides a reliable, endogenously tagged red fluorescent peroxisome marker for investigating peroxisome dynamics, metabolic regulation, and organelle contact sites in vivo .",
